WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.081
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.081 --> 00:00:09.930
Honorable leadership is
about living up to duty.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.610
When we're given a promotion and put into
a position of greater formal leadership

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.790
responsibility, that that is often
because we've done well at something and

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.150
our potential has been
positively evaluated.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.470
So if you have a set of different people,
and

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.830
some of them are seen as having
greater potential than others,

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:35.220
perhaps they've been more accomplished
than others, then you would expect

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.760
them to be put into a position of
responsibility and leadership.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.970
But if you think about it, that causes
all of us to see that promotion

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:48.490
as a reward, not as a duty.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.950
Compare that to a world
where we see a promotion or

00:00:54.950 --> 00:01:00.140
other kind of granting of leadership
responsibility as a very solemn

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.475
duty that we have been
asked to live up to.

00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:08.620
When we face leadership responsibilities,

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.650
we're asked to do things
that are difficult.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:17.977
We're asked to resolve tensions
that will require trade offs.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.790
That will require that
we make tough decisions.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.480
And whenever we do that we
are being challenged to live up

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.500
to the duty of our office.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.450
There are exceptional leaders
who perhaps didn't go and

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.120
take 100% market share or add a billion
dollars of revenue but day in and

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.840
day out we're willing to confront and
deal with the most difficult situations.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.120
And I know right now you
can think of such leaders,

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.490
I challenge you to be such a leader.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:54.030
&gt;&gt; No leader is without opportunity
to grow, so where do you want to go?

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.507
Explore Stanford's upcoming programs.

00:01:56.507 --> 00:02:00.209
[MUSIC]

